       ppnnmmttoorraasstt [--ssttaannddaarrdd|--rrllee] [_p_n_m_f_i_l_e]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnmmttoorraassttreads  a  PPM  image as input and produces a Sun rasterfile as
       output.

       Color values in Sun rasterfiles are eight bits wide, so ppnnmmttoorraasstt  will
       automatically  scale colors to have a maxval of 255.  An extra ppaammddeepptthh
       step is not necessary.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppnnmmttoorraasstt recognizes the
       following command line options:

       All options can be abbreviated to their shortest unique prefix.



       --ssttaannddaarrdd

              Forces the result to be in RT_STANDARD form.


       --rrllee

              Forces the result to be in  RT_BYTE_ENCODED,  which  is  smaller
              but, well, less standard.

              The default is --rrllee.




